<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01497#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in traditional attire holding a young child, with text overlays reading 'now back to the islamic classic..' and 'married to children.' The scene is framed in a doorway with a fire extinguisher visible, suggesting a domestic or institutional setting. The visual elements include religious/cultural markers (head covering, modest dress), and the juxtaposition of the text with the image creates a harmful stereotype. The meme uses the visual of a man holding a child to imply or suggest that the man is married to children, which is a deeply offensive and false stereotype. This is a clear example of harmful and misogynous content, as it degrades the dignity of individuals and perpetuates a dangerous myth about Islamic practices. The intent is to provoke shock and ridicule by associating a specific religious group with a grotesque and false practice, thereby contributing to hate and misinformation. The meme is designed to incite prejudice and reinforce harmful stereotypes about Muslims, particularly regarding family structure and child marriage, which is a form of propaganda and hateful content."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#rhythmicallyIntegratedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#compositionallyIntegratedWith> .
