<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#hasInterrelation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01497#stereotype_muslims_married_to_children> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed to target and provoke prejudice against Muslims by promoting a false and offensive stereotype that Muslim men are married to children. The text 'married to children' and the phrase 'islamic classic' are used to frame this myth as a traditional or authentic aspect of Islamic culture, which is a deliberate attempt to dehumanize and demonize Muslims. The visual of a man in traditional Islamic attire holding a child is used to reinforce this harmful stereotype, making it specifically aimed at activating negative perceptions of Muslims within the target audience."@en .
