<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#CausalRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One dimension being causally related with another in memes, e.g. text explaining why visual situation exists"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01497#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'married to children' is overlaid on the image of the man holding a child, creating an analogical mapping where the man is implicitly identified as being 'married to children'. This is a harmful stereotype that falsely attributes the practice of child marriage to Islamic men, using the visual of the man holding a child to imply a sexual or marital relationship that is not supported by Islamic teachings or reality. The mapping is established through the juxtaposition of the text with the visual material, where the man's role as a caregiver is distorted into a stereotype of predatory marriage."@en .
