<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Textual Material elements from the image. Textual Material includes: captions, text overlays, speech bubbles, written words, phrases, sentences, and any visible text. For each textual element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'main_caption', 'speech_bubble_text'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the main caption', 'the speech bubble text'), 3) A brief description of the text content and its context. Focus on all visible text elements that contribute to the meme's meaning. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"main_caption\", \"label\": \"the main caption\", \"description\": \"The text 'This is fine' written in bold letters at the bottom of the image\"}"@en .
_:n1ebee3eb46024fa8958a643a8987362ab104 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
